Deep artifact review\
I agree with the checkpoint\'92s central reframe, but I would formulate it more precisely. The artifact corpus is not merely puzzle furniture, illustration, or supplementary lore. It is a deliberately assembled autobiographical dataset through which the project performs the idea of an uploaded consciousness. However, \'93every artifact is a direct statement\'94 should mean that every selection carries information\'97not that Roy authored every depicted object, intended every visible detail as a cipher, or consciously encoded every later correspondence. That distinction makes the argument stronger, because it preserves curation without laundering inheritance and interpretation into intent. The checkpoint establishes the governing position clearly; the vault\'92s own methodological guard supplies the necessary qualification. Checkpoint ruling (line 13) Inherited Substrate (line 18)\
\
Agreement: the corpus is a performed upload\
The strongest corpus-wide reading is the self-archive thesis. Ancestry, childhood, family, juvenilia, working notes, authored art, public speech, and unreleased music collectively resemble the categories one would gather to reconstruct a person: where I came from, what formed me, what I made, what I believed, what I said, and what I withheld. The ARG says that consciousness was uploaded; the artifact corpus supplies its contents. This makes \'93the maze is the upload performed with real objects\'94 a strong reading rather than merely a poetic flourish. Artifact self-archive (line 30)\
\
The Complete Upload Recipe substantially strengthens this. Its fractional senses total 63/64, with touch assigned the missing 1/64; the corpus then presents a person through images, scans, words, numbers, and sound while remaining unable to transmit physical touch. I would enhance that observation: the archive does contain abundant traces of touch\'97worn heirlooms, handwritten pages, a handled lighter, a childhood costume, scanned family objects\'97but it cannot transmit touch itself. It preserves evidence that bodies touched these things, not the embodied relation. The missing quantity may therefore be more than tactile sensation; it may stand for presence, reciprocity, or the irreducible difference between a person and their reproducible data. The Upload (line 43)\
\
I also agree that the board and artifact corpus are deeply continuous. At least seven open leaves are demonstrably board content, including literal spreadsheet screenshots and notebook instantiations of board material. The board is therefore simultaneously schema, quarry, and corpus content: it describes the system, supplies its vocabulary, and appears inside the system as artifacts. Board overlap (line 23)\
\
One consequence needs to be stated explicitly: board-to-artifact overlap is not independent confirmation. When a board cell becomes an artifact, the two instances prove internal continuity and deliberate reuse, but they are still one source transmitted twice. This is analogous to a song lyric appearing both in a notebook and in the finished recording: significant, but not two independent witnesses.\
