Enhancement: \'93source code\'94 should become a layered model\
The computational metaphor becomes much cleaner if the layers are separated. The board is the schema or ontology: its ladders, cycles, principles, taxonomies, and upload instructions describe how the system thinks. The artifacts are the training corpus or state capture: autobiographical examples, memories, inherited objects, sketches, statements, and musical fragments. The codes are pointers and edges that bind items into authored chains. The maze is the runtime and community interface. SARAVI is the digital-double or model-interface produced from the upload premise, while the music and later character work are outputs performed from the same underlying material.\
