Deep synthesis: the archive is a version history of relations\
The artifacts do not merely confirm the Field Guide\'92s existing cosmology. They change its center of gravity. The Hall is best understood not as a static copy of Roy\'92s finished consciousness, but as an attempt to preserve how that consciousness was formed: through family, inherited objects, other people\'92s voices, books and images, bodily experience, ambition, failure, revision, music-making, and the audience that receives and transforms it.\
\
I therefore agree with the core self-archive thesis, but I would revise its strongest sentence. The defensible formulation is:\
\
Every artifact is direct evidence of Roy\'92s selection, but not every word, voice, image, or idea inside an artifact is Roy-authored. Every placement is a curatorial statement; the selected content may be inherited, collaborative, quoted, found, provisional, contradicted, or later revised.\
\
That distinction is not a qualification around the edge. It is the key to what kind of self the Hall preserves. The Hall does not represent an autonomous mind generating itself from nothing; it represents a consciousness made out of relations.\
\
