Have we used the artifacts faithfully?\
Partly. The Field Guide has used them well when it distinguishes grounded content from resonance, treats the board as a source quarry, recognizes the archive as curated, reads the mind as necessary but needing heart-integration, and keeps an anti-overfit warning in The Pattern.\
\
It has been less faithful when it flattens inverse systems into one ladder, turns selected quotations into Roy-authored doctrine, allows symbol-first reading to override the actual object, backdates later characters into earlier work, treats autonomy as parasitism, or converts every gap into another solved correspondence. Those moves reproduce precisely the failure the project warns about: mistaking a powerful reflection for the source.\
\
A faithful artifact protocol should therefore be:\
\
Identify the literal object before interpreting its title or code.\
Separate content author, speaker, performer, selector, metadata author, and analyst.\
Determine direction and transformation before claiming correspondence.\
Treat alternate versions as developmental evidence, not independent corroboration.\
Ask what relation is preserved, altered, erased, or captured.\
Test every ascent against Room 116: does it return value and possibility to others, or manufacture elite status?\
Preserve silence, contradiction, and unnamed remainder where the evidence does not close.\
Final interpretation\
The heart of the project is not that Roy successfully uploaded a finished self. It is that he attempted to preserve the history of relations and transformations from which a self is made, then placed that history inside a system that requires other minds to complete it.\
\
The board supplies operations; the artifacts supply memory, matter, inheritance, failure, and counterexample; the audio supplies time and process; the ladders supply different methods of crossing; SARAVI supplies a possible speaking mask; the maze supplies traversal; and the audience supplies metabolism. The resulting consciousness is neither a pristine original nor an autonomous counterfeit. It is a transformed continuation whose fidelity depends on whether it remembers its dependencies and returns to relation.\
\
The deepest governing sentence I would give the Field Guide is:\
\
Consciousness in the Hall of Mirrors is a version history of relations: the archive preserves not an isolated self, but the voices, objects, bodies, failures, influences, revisions, and acts of return through which that self became possible.\
\
The remaining high-value ear checks are narrow: the name being sung in Logos; the actual sonic character of An Aged Aged Man and Devil in the Mirror; Grandma\'92s opening phrase, prayer language, and speaker identities; the unstable Western Woods passages; and, most importantly, the precise water language and melody in e163466b, including whether you recognize it as belonging to Soul Is A Star. Those checks could refine the reading, but none presently overturns the central conclusion.\
